1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,507
A Kenyan presidential aspirant just told Nigerian billionaire Aliko Dangote to pack his bags.

2
00:00:05,507 --> 00:00:11,462
Patrick Osoi said that once he is sworn in, in twenty twenty-seven, Dangote will be heading back to Nigeria.

3
00:00:11,462 --> 00:00:15,660
This is about Dangote's planned sixteen billion dollar refinery in Lamu.

4
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:18,691
Everyone expected Nigerians to fight back.

5
00:00:18,691 --> 00:00:20,141
Instead?

6
00:00:20,142 --> 00:00:22,772
If you want to chase him, chase him.

7
00:00:22,771 --> 00:00:25,389
We never benefited from him anyway.

8
00:00:25,389 --> 00:00:28,019
Dangote should fight his own battles.

9
00:00:28,019 --> 00:00:29,599
And this one.

10
00:00:29,599 --> 00:00:33,479
Now Dangote has no option but to fund his opponent's campaign.

11
00:00:33,479 --> 00:00:37,477
Remember, this is a campaign promise, not government policy.

12
00:00:37,476 --> 00:00:39,493
So who won this round?

13
00:00:39,493 --> 00:00:41,969
Full story on NEXTSCENE TV.
